      "message": "BIP-352: add test vectors for skipped inputs and label edge cases\n\nSix send and receive vectors for cases the file does not cover yet:\n- inputs of ineligible types (P2WSH, P2MS, P2PK, empty scriptPubKey)\n  beside an eligible one;\n- P2SH-P2WSH, P2TR with an empty witness, and a P2TR output key that is\n  not on the curve, all skipped;\n- a P2TR script path spend whose internal key is not NUMS, which counts;\n- a P2PKH whose pubkey hash matches 33 bytes that are not a valid key;\n- the largest label, 0xFFFFFFFF;\n- two recipients, one with a labeled address listed after the other\n  recipient, with a taproot and a non-taproot input.\n\nThe P2WSH and P2SH-P2WSH witness script is also a valid compressed key,\nso an implementation that reads the last witness item as a key fails.\n\nreference.py computed the expected values and passes on the whole file.\n\nAssisted-by: my usual tools (LLM, Internet, computer). Mistakes are mine.\nSigned-off-by: Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net>",
